  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xf6;ster f&#xf6;r Fred- Regional sudanesisk dialog</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voices for Peace- Regional Sudanese Dialogue</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The projects overall goal is &quot;an inclusive, influential Sudanese civil society builds momentum around peaceful solutions to the conflict, within Sudan and regionally.&quot;

Underlying the main objective of trying to support a more inclusive and influential civil society are three outcomes: 

1) Enhanced capacities and cohesion among engaged civil society actors, including those inside (internally) and outside Sudan (regionally), with a particular focus on women and youth.

2) Enhanced community and civil society participation in political dialogue and mediation processes at local, national, regional, and international levels, with emphasis on the meaningful engagement of women and youth.

3) An increasingly strong digital constituency for peace.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinnor och ungdomar utg&#xf6;r den demografiska majoriten av den sudanesiska befolkningen och har spelat en betydelsefull roll in de politiska demonstrationerna for fredlig och demokratisk f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring. Dessa grupper &#xe4;r ocks&#xe5; de mest utsatta och utg&#xf6;r dessutom majoriteten av befolkningen som flytt Sudan. 

Fredsskapande i Sudan har ett arv av elitistism som inte lyckats f&#xf6;rankra en fredlig eller demokratisk utveckling. Behovet av att v&#xe4;nda sig till bredare grupper i samh&#xe4;llet i fredsarbetet framst&#xe5;r som en n&#xf6;dv&#xe4;ndig &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rd. 

Denna insats har sin utg&#xe5;ngspunkt i att fred inte kan tvingas fram eller vinnas p&#xe5; slagf&#xe4;ltet. Det fredsfr&#xe4;mjande arbetet beh&#xf6;ver vila p&#xe5; ett bredare deltagande &#xe4;n hitills och en politisk konsensus som tar i h&#xe4;nsyn ett bredare folkligt perspektiv. 

Denna insats tar riktning p&#xe5; kvinnors och ungdomars outnyttjade potential att konstruktivt bidra till det sudanesiska fredsarbetet och utveckla en regional dialog och etablera kontakter med AU, regionala institutioner och andra plattformar som har det formella medlingsuppdraget.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and young people make up the demographic majority of the Sudanese population and have played a significant role in the political demonstrations for peaceful and democratic change. These groups are also the most vulnerable and also make up the majority of the population who have fled Sudan. 
Peacemaking in Sudan has a legacy of elitism that has failed to anchor peaceful or democratic development. The need to reach out to broader groups in society in peace work appears to be a necessary measure. 
This effort is based on the fact that peace cannot be forced or won on the battlefield. Peace-promoting work needs to rest on broader participation than hitherto and a political consensus that takes into account a broader popular perspective. 
This effort addresses the untapped potential of women and young people to contribute constructively to Sudanese peace efforts and to develop a regional dialogue and establish contacts with the AU, regional institutions and other platforms that have the formal mediation mission.</narrative>
  </description>
